# Lua short strings: no raw newlines

JA3 loads mod Lua and reports **unfinished string** if a `"..."` or `'...'` short string spans a real line break.

## Required

- Multiline `AdditionalHint` / `Description` / `T(...)` text: use `\n` on **one** physical line, or long brackets `[[...]]` / `[=[...] =]`.
- Never press Enter inside an open `"..."` / `'...'` when editing `InventoryItem/*.lua`, `items.lua`, or other loaded Lua.

## Good

```lua
AdditionalHint = T(123, "... first line\n... second line"),
```

## Bad (mod fails to load)

```lua
AdditionalHint = T(123, "... first line
... second line"),
```

## Gate

`scripts/check-lua-quoted-strings.ps1` (Quality gates CI) fails the build on this pattern.
